From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: Avoid duplicate Trek Tech hotspot dispatch

The command-result compatibility patch preserves QTVR mouseOver's return value
until the title reads `the result`. Trek Tech's original mPanMaster handler then
calls hotHitPlay for an undefined object hotspot. Do not also call hotHitPlay
inside the XObject: doing both can queue an exit transit twice and leave the
second arrival without a live panorama object.
---
 engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp | 14 +-------------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
--- a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
@@ -261,20 +261,8 @@ void QTVR::m_mouseOver(int nargs) {
 
 				if (nodeChanged || (hotspotData && hotspotData->type == MKTAG('l','i','n','k')))
 					g_lingo->push(Common::String::format("jump,%d", node));
-				else {
-					// The TNG Technical Manual's Director 4 bytecode invokes mouseOver
-					// as a command, then dispatches the selected object through its movie
-					// handlers. The rollover callback has already populated
-					// prevIndex/validSpotFlag. Run only the playback handler here: a
-					// second hotHitReport for the same hotspot toggles validSpotFlag off,
-					// making an ordinary stationary click fail while a drag appears to work.
-					if (Common::String(g_director->getGameId()).equals("trektech")) {
-						int cframe = g_lingo->_state->callstack.size();
-						LC::call("hotHitPlay", 0, false);
-						g_lingo->execute(cframe);
-					}
+				else
 					g_lingo->push(Common::String::format("%s,%d", hotspotData ? tag2str((uint32)hotspotData->type) : "undf", hotspot));
-				}
 
 				return;
 			}
